                <pb facs="0352" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-03T16:00:00+02:00">April 3, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 5—5:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>180. Department’s 67, March 31, 4 p.m., concerning American mission personnel at
                    Addis Ababa. The British Embassy states that this matter has been brought to the
                    attention of the appropriate military authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
